# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored; .env.example is not.
#
#   cp .env.example .env && chmod 600 .env
#
# A real environment variable always wins over this file, so
# `DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=other make run-deepseek` still overrides it.
# Values are used literally: $OTHER is NOT expanded, and quotes are only needed
# when a value contains spaces or a '#'.

# ── which model provider ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# anthropic (default) | deepseek | scripted
OBA_BACKEND=deepseek

# Needed when OBA_BACKEND=deepseek. Create one at platform.deepseek.com.
# There is no other credential source for this provider, so startup refuses
# without it.
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=

# Needed when OBA_BACKEND=anthropic, unless `ant auth login` has been run.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Model ids default from OBA_BACKEND and rarely need setting. An id belonging to
# a different provider is refused at startup rather than silently remapped.
# OBA_AGENT_MODEL=deepseek-v4-pro
# OBA_CLASSIFIER_MODEL=deepseek-v4-flash

# ── how answers read ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# zh-CN (default) | en | match  — "match" mirrors whatever the person wrote in.
OBA_REPLY_LANGUAGE=zh-CN

# ── looking things up outside the corpus ────────────────────────────────────
# The official service directory ships enabled and needs nothing.
# Live web search returns current openings AND courses nationwide; it is OFF
# until a key is set, and startup logs LIVE_SEARCH_DISABLED when it is.
#
# The default vendor is bocha (博查), because these searches are for Chinese
# cities on Chinese-language sites. Set the key and nothing else.
# OBA_SEARCH_API_KEY=
#
# The two vendors answer DIFFERENT wire shapes — bocha takes a POST with a
# bearer token, brave takes a GET with a header — so the provider is named
# explicitly and never guessed from the URL. Pointing the URL at one vendor
# while the provider says the other fails SILENTLY: the request is accepted,
# nothing parses, and the city reads as empty.
# OBA_SEARCH_PROVIDER=bocha
# OBA_SEARCH_API_URL=https://api.bochaai.com/v1/web-search
#
# For brave instead, all three lines have to change together:
# OBA_SEARCH_PROVIDER=brave
# OBA_SEARCH_API_URL=https://api.search.brave.com/res/v1/web/search
# OBA_SEARCH_KEY_HEADER=X-Subscription-Token

# ── read-aloud ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Answers are ALWAYS readable aloud: with nothing set here the browser uses its
# own built-in voice, which needs no key and no network. These variables replace
# that with a vendor voice.
#
# Off unless keyed, deliberately. A feature that silently degrades is worse than
# one that says it is not switched on; startup logs TTS_DISABLED when there is
# no key.
#
# !! READ THIS BEFORE POINTING IT AT REAL USERS.
# The default backbone is Fish's FREE model, and Fish's published terms for it
# say requests may be used to improve model quality. The text sent is the
# ANSWER — it names the person's city, their employment situation, and often the
# benefit they are trying to claim. That is the price of the free tier, and it is
# a privacy decision, not a billing one. The paid backbones (s2.1-pro, s2-pro,
# s1) bill at $0.015 per 1,000 UTF-8 bytes, which for Chinese is 3 bytes a
# character — roughly $0.018 for a typical answer. See docs/17-read-aloud.md.
#
# OBA_TTS_API_KEY=              # fish.audio/app/api-keys — free to create
# OBA_TTS_VOICE_ID=             # the model id from the voice's fish.audio URL
# OBA_TTS_MODEL=s2.1-pro-free   # s2.1-pro-free (default, free) | s2.1-pro | s2-pro | s1
# OBA_TTS_API_URL=              # override the endpoint; defaults to Fish's

# ── everything else has a working default ───────────────────────────────────
# OBA_ADDR=:8787
# OBA_STATE_PATH=.state/oba.json
# OBA_K_ANONYMITY=5
# OBA_ENABLED_INTENTS=individual_pathway,low_access_support

# ── accounts ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Everything except /api/health and the sign-in endpoints requires an account.
# OBA_INVITE_CODES is comma-separated and EMPTY MEANS SIGN-UP IS CLOSED — an
# unconfigured deployment must refuse new accounts, not admit everybody.
# OBA_DEMO_ACCOUNT adopts subjects left behind from before accounts existed.
# OBA_INVITE_CODES=
# OBA_DEMO_ACCOUNT=demo
# OBA_SIGNIN_TTL_DAYS=30
